1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,320
Jarir Ibn Abdullah, the companion of the Prophet -pbuh-

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:07,280
When he saw a horse and offered to buy it from its owner

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:11,600
For how much? for 80 Usually, how does bargaining work?

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:16,160
When you say 80, I try to take it for 70

5
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:20,000
But when Jarir asked him and he replied that it was for 80

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,520
Jarir then asks him if he'd take 100 for it

7
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,520
He agrees...

8
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:26,520
But he kept increasing the price until it reached 300

9
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:29,560
He raised the price up to 300 Dirham

10
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,440
He raised the price up to 300 Dirham

11
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,680
And the man was in disbelief

12
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:38,680
And he sold it for 300 and quickly left without looking back

13
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,960
He feared that he might rethink himself

14
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:44,000
So, he was asked about why he did that?

15
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,960
He told you it was for 80, why not buy it for that price?

16
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:50,360
He said "I saw that this horse is worth 300"

17
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:55,560
"And I gave oath to the Prophet to give advice to all Muslims"
